From: Meerzulee and Linux psX contributors
Subject: [PATCH] net: psx_mts preserve returned TX word0 until descriptor reuse

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Candidate for a bounded fresh-boot comparison, not a confirmed stall fix.
The retained FW12.02 completion contract checks COWN and the word2 sentinel,
then frees its tracked packet and restores the word2 sentinel. It does not
clear descriptor word0 at that retirement point (raw252ce2..252d77).

Omit only the extra Linux word0 clear. The next mts_xmit assigns the complete
new status/length/EOR fields before its OWN-last release. Buffer retention,
software ledger, accounting, polling and every lifecycle guard are unchanged.
No firmware bytes are included. Existing GPL-2.0-only source notices remain.

Base-SHA256: fa1e0181ca11e9e21fea509b14654c0e37788d537f1664f598dec6dca4bfda79  drivers/net/ethernet/psx_mts_net.c
Result-SHA256: 8a1f0b9a351099e1dae454f7d35d84f26abc0784b89fd47c24fe77241b0d45bf  drivers/net/ethernet/psx_mts_net.c

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/psx_mts_net.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/psx_mts_net.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/psx_mts_net.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/psx_mts_net.c
@@ -559,7 +559,6 @@
 		if (!mts_tx_retire(&s->tx, d0, d2, &length))
 			break;
 		WRITE_ONCE(ring[slot].word[2], cpu_to_le32(MTS_TX_SENTINEL));
-		WRITE_ONCE(ring[slot].word[0], cpu_to_le32(mts_tx_idle(slot)));
 		packets++;
 		bytes += length;
 	}
